  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education and Livelihoods for Girls and Women (Ethiopia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girls and disabled children in Ethiopia often never go to school. This is especially so in poor families and in rural areas. Girls that start school often drop out because families need them to work, or because of early marriage. Provision of education for disabled children is scarce. This project will provide training to teachers to enable them to work with disabled children, and support schools to make them more accessible. Loans to families will generate sufficient income so that children are not forced to work. The project will engage parents and community leaders to discuss the importance of education to children. Part of these community discussions will focus on the practice of early marriage, and the practice of genital mutilation. As a result, thousands of girls and disabled children who have never been to school, or who would have dropped out, will receive a basic education. The project also aims to reduce the incidence of early marriage and genital mutilation.</narrative>
  </description>
